# 🌎 washington-lulc-ml-landsat.git

Sharing scripts created in UCLA MAGIST's GEOG 415: Geospatial Data Science Futures. Collaborative final project: ML LULC classification for Eastern Washington with my classmates.

Random forest land cover classification of Washington State from Landsat 8 and 9 surface reflectance, trained on ground truth points pooled from the whole class, in Google Earth Engine (Spring 2025, Dr. Bo Zhou).

Each student digitized seasonal ground truth for one Landsat WRS-2 path/row and year. I digitized 600 points for path 43, row 27 (Spokane and the Palouse, 2024), then pooled 17 of the class's collections into one training set covering 13 WRS-2 footprints (paths 43–48, rows 26–28) and the years 2014–2024. The model classifies six land cover classes: urban, agriculture, rangeland, forest, water, and barren.

## Scripts

Run in order; each script's header names the original class script it came from.

| Script | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| [`01_sceneSelection`](./01_sceneSelection) | Filters Landsat 8 and 9 Collection 2 Level 2 by path/row and season to find cloud-free 2024 scenes |
| [`02_groundTruth/p43_r27/`](./02_groundTruth/p43_r27) | Thirteen digitization scripts, one per scene: hand-placed points for six classes, about 150 per season (600 total) |
| [`03_mergeGroundTruth`](./03_mergeGroundTruth) | Merges the 13 scene collections into one exported FeatureCollection |
| [`04_poolClassGroundTruth`](./04_poolClassGroundTruth) | Pools the class's collections: converts polygon sets to centroids, repairs property names and types, drops two collections missing date and path/row, screens coordinate errors, joins each point to its source scene, masks clouds, and samples reflectance |
| [`05_harmonizeAndSample`](./05_harmonizeAndSample) | Coerces the pooled schema to consistent types and re-samples six bands at 30 m |
| [`06_randomForest`](./06_randomForest) | Adds Tasseled Cap components, tests 30–150 m sampling scales, tunes the random forest, assesses accuracy, and classifies 2017 and 2022 summer composites for change detection |
| [`07_lulcMap`](./07_lulcMap) | Map of the 2022 classification with a legend, plus the gallery thumbnail |
| [`tools`](./tools) | Shared functions used by `05` and `06`: scene join, QA_PIXEL cloud mask, reflectance scaling, sampling |

## Results

- **Scale sensitivity.** 30 m sampling with Tasseled Cap components scored best (0.709, vs 0.687 for the six reflectance bands alone); accuracy fell steadily at coarser scales.
- **Tuning.** Earth Engine memory limits ruled out a grid search, so hyperparameters were tuned one at a time: 130 trees, 3 variables per split, minimum leaf population 1, bag fraction 0.5.
- **Accuracy.** About 68–70% overall on a random 80/20 train/test split (kappa about 0.62–0.63). The committed `06_randomForest` reports 68.3%. The exact figure depends on which points land in the test set, and Earth Engine reshuffles that split whenever upstream code changes; earlier versions of the same model scored 70.2% and 69.1% (details in the script's comments). Forest and water classify well (producer's accuracy about 0.88 and 0.92); rangeland is the weakest class (about 0.40), confused mostly with agriculture and barren.
- **Change detection.** Classified 2017 and 2022 summer median composites for path 46, row 27 (Seattle to the Cascades) and built a transition matrix. `06` maps stable pixels in grey and changed pixels in the color of their 2022 class.

## Notes

- Classmates' ground truth asset paths are withheld in `04`, and the steps that need them are commented out. The pooled and sampled results load from my own public exports, so every script runs as-is.
- The ground truth file and variable names say `r43_p27`, but they mean path 43, row 27 (the labels are swapped).
- To open the scripts in the Code Editor: https://code.earthengine.google.com/?accept_repo=users/leependu/washington-lulc-ml-landsat

This README was drafted by Claude Opus 5.5. [`tools`](./tools) and [`07_lulcMap`](./07_lulcMap) were written with Claude Opus 5.5, which also helped clean up the original class scripts in October 2026.

Setting up GitHub mirror:

```
git clone https://earthengine.googlesource.com/users/leependu/washington-lulc-ml-landsat
git remote add github git@github.com:leependu/washington-lulc-ml-landsat.git
git config remote.github.push refs/heads/master:refs/heads/main
```
